DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 6:00 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 5:45 PM.\nOn stage: 7:00 PM–7:45 PM.\nACT I 
 Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — pr
 oduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time danc
 ers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Tim
 e.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiv
 ing and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are cal
 led unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedul
 e\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mast
 er: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N
 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Infantry ***\nSoldie
 rs: Artillery\, Brigade\, Infantry — Costume (you provide): Black Seam
 less Tights\, Black Camisole Leotard Male Soldiers: Black T-shirt\, Blac
 k tights\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair
 : High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): White Gloves\; Prop (B
 A provides): Brown gun\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Powde
 r matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease wi
 th an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara.
  No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so da
 ncer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark Red
  lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ba
 llet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with ca
 re while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly no
 tify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of disc
 overy\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessori
 es on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain 
 from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\
 , mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply st
 age make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from s
 mudging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use 
 of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment
  not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or bever
 age while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove co
 stumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remov
 e all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use
 \n• Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully wit
 h any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do no
 t pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or 
 stain costumes.
